From f0114049758d0e146b063a9095778c61e839cee9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alberto Gallegos <alberto.gallegos.muro@intel.com>
Date: Tue, 21 Jul 2026 17:56:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add XPU support to FBGEMM TBE training tests

Retrofit the forward and backward TBE training tests so they exercise the
XPU implementations of `dense_embedding_codegen_lookup_function` and
`split_embedding_codegen_lookup_rowwise_adagrad_function_pt2` when only
`fbgemm-gpu-cpu` (CPU wheel) and `fbgemm-xpu` (XPU op registrations)
are installed - i.e. no CUDA device is present.

The XPU kernels implement only the no-bag / unweighted / non-VBE /
non-GWD / uniform-B / non-cache surface, so the patch:

- Registers `fbgemm_xpu` from `fbgemm_gpu/test/test_utils.py` and
  extends `gpu_available` / `gpu_unavailable` / `use_cpu_strategy()`
  to treat XPU as a GPU accelerator (unblocking the
  `@skipIf(*gpu_unavailable)` decorators).
- Routes `fbgemm_gpu.tbe.utils.common.to_device(..., use_cpu=False)` to
  `xpu` when CUDA is unavailable (source-side patch).
- Adds a `fbgemm_gpu/test/conftest.py` that monkey-patches the installed
  wheel's `to_device` (and the re-exports in `tbe.utils.__init__`,
  `tbe.utils.offsets`, `tbe.utils.quantize`) so tests running against
  the `fbgemm-gpu-cpu` wheel also route non-CPU tensors to XPU.
- Introduces per-file `_SplitCodegenForXPU` / `_DenseCodegenForXPU`
  shims that build the codegen modules in CPU / HOST layout and then
  reshape the internal state onto XPU (5-tensor weights list where
  index 0 is `weights_dev`) so the AutogradXPU op dispatch is hit.
- Narrows the hypothesis parameter space through `assume(...)` filters
  and coerces XPU-incompatible parameters inside `execute_forward_`
  (`use_cache=False`, `use_experimental_tbe=False`, `pooling_mode=NONE`,
  `weighted=False`, `mixed=False`, `mixed_B=False`, unsupported
  dtypes remapped) so a single hypothesis example is enough to
  exercise the target op.  Because `use_cache` is coerced to False,
  the UVM-cache forward tests (fp16, fp32) reduce to the no-cache
  path on XPU and are exercised without being skipped.
- Skips CUDA-only forward tests that call `torch.cuda.*` primitives or
  exercise features (FP8, raw embedding streaming, fused pooled quant,
  FP16-large grid) that are not implemented on XPU.
- Disables `bounds_check_indices` inside the XPU codegen shim
  (`BoundsCheckMode.NONE`) because the bounds-check op has no XPU
  kernel today.
- Filters out one CPU-wheel limitation (BF16 output for the CPU no-bag
  forward) that is now sampled because `use_cpu_strategy()` returns
  `booleans()`.

CUDA and CPU-only behaviour is preserved.

Signed-off-by: Alberto Gallegos <alberto.gallegos.muro@intel.com>
